Renders poisonous corpses, etc. noticeably less dangerous -- one of the
big reasons not to eat poisonous things to get PR is because of the stat
drain.  A unicorn horn currently completely negates the issue, but you
have to find one first.  Being able to meditate and restore stats pretty
much knocks that problem out of the way, too.

Becomes meaningless once you have a unicorn horn; advancing to "basic"
is no longer worthwhile at that point, so is wasted slots unless...

> At skilled, the player benefits from further enhancements to the ease
> and efectiveness as from unskilled>basic, but also gets quicker
> health/ mana regeneration while meditating as well as full
> enlightenment and stat-restore.

Seriously overpowered combined with a burned or engraved Elbereth and a
blindfold.

> it comes with drawbacks: Time spent sat around meditating is time
> burning nutrition, and there is a risk of getting eaten before you can

Nutrition isn't really a problem in Nethack, though, and given that you
can sit on Elbereth and be immune to danger, I'm not sure this really
adds anything to the game.

On the opposite end of the scale, if it takes you so long to come out of 
a meditative state that you lose 3/4 of your HP to one elf beating on
you, then it isn't even worth doing.

